# Association plugin project rule

Read `AGENTS.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, and the relevant files under `docs/` before making architectural changes.

Hard rules:

- Do not equate members with `wp_users`.
- Do not build a mandatory external service.
- Do not add telemetry, ads, hidden callbacks or trackers.
- Do not make product architecture depend on a paid upsell.
- Preserve history rather than overwriting it.
- Treat finalized/adjusted minutes as immutable historical revisions.
- Use capabilities and least privilege.
- Treat member data as personal data.
- Do not implement bookkeeping, payroll, ERP, advanced booking or sports-specific competition management as part of the core MVP.
- Do not use Custom Post Types by default without evaluating the data's properties.
- Do not introduce a new dependency without documenting why it is needed, how it is maintained and what happens if it disappears.
- Prefer WordPress APIs where they fit, but do not force unsuitable domain data into WordPress posts/users merely to avoid custom tables.

Before coding a major subsystem, ensure its product/domain model is documented and the relevant open questions have been resolved.
